    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Penitent Host",
    "summary": "At the start of each battle round, you may choose one Vow of Atonement for your army; it lasts until the next battle round starts, and each vow can be chosen only once per battle. The Path of the Penitent: your PENITENT models get +3\" Move. Absolution in Battle: when one of your units is picked to fight after making a Charge move that turn, melee weapons of its PENITENT models get +1 Attacks and +1 Strength until the phase ends. Death Before Disgrace: when a melee attack destroys one of your PENITENT models that has not yet fought this phase, roll a D6; on a 2+ it stays in play, may fight once the attacking unit's attacks are finished, and is then removed.",
